        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 6:08 p.m. Central Daylight Time Wednesday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for North Central Manitoba. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: South Indian Lake, Amisk Provincial Park, Thompson, Thicket Portage, Pikwitonei and Nelson House. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds and large hail are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
